+++| Finding | Remediation | Where |
+++|---|---|---|
+++| R1 the followed selection survived the collection's close, so the same collection re-opened with its persisted selection left the editor blank | Following the core's selection is scoped to one open collection: the followed id is forgotten whenever the collection's id changes (closed, or another opened), so the re-opened collection's selected request is opened again. The stale-snapshot protection is unchanged (the draft test still passes). Test: close the collection, push the closed snapshot, push the same board; the URL field and the selected tab return and `openRequest` was sent once more | `api-client.tsx`, `api-client.test.tsx` |
+++| R2 folders rendered flat: collapsing one hid only its direct requests, and a folder counted none of its descendants | The tree is a hierarchy: every folder (listed, implied by a request's path or by a deeper folder) has its child folders and its direct requests under it; a collapsed folder hides its whole subtree; a folder's count is every request under it (the prototype's `visible(parent)` walk and descendant counts). Search still lists matches flat, collapsed or not. Test: nested `products/runtime` under `products`, counts 2 and 1, collapsing the parent hides the child folder and both requests, search finds the nested request, collapsing the child alone hides only its request | `request-tree.tsx`, `api-client.test.tsx` |
+++| R3 a tool opened from the Collection menu lost its opener (the menu item closed with the menu), so the sheet returned focus to the body | `Modal` takes an explicit surviving `returnFocus` target, preferred over whatever had focus at mount; the tools sheet passes the Collection chip. The menu's own Escape also returns focus to the chip. Test: keyboard open (Enter on the chip, Tab to Environments…, Enter), close by Escape and by the close control, focus back on the chip each time; Escape on the open menu too | `modal.tsx`, `tools-sheet.tsx`, `api-client.tsx`, `api-client.test.tsx` |
+++| R4 a send from an already dirty (or new) request left its completion standing through the next edits, since only a change of the dirty flag cleared the status line | Every edit settles the status line (an action still in flight keeps its word); the dirty-flag effect stays for metadata changes the core reports without an edit here. Tests: send from a dirty request, then edit: "Unsaved changes"; send from a new request, then edit: "New · not saved yet" | `request-editor.tsx`, `api-client.test.tsx` |
+++| E1 no native evidence that the tools sheet returns focus to the chip | N01 now opens Environments from the keyboard twice (Space on the chip, Tab to Environments…, Space) and closes it by Escape and by the close control, asserting from the AX tree that focus returned to `Collection Topics API` each time (`sheet_focus_back`, trees `api-focus-escape`, `api-focus-button`); the inventory text names it | `acceptance_c41.py`, `native-checks.json` |
